r of languages and speak  them i mean there are some people here  who speak too yeah and and want to  almost apologize for the fact that they  only speak english language they  shouldn't and everybody is very  supportive and and respectful of the  fact that people dif people have  different approaches but the same goal  exactly not even the same goal some  people want to become totally fluent  some people just want to have an  understanding of the language and that's  all fine and so um you know the next  time there's a polyglot gathering near  you and the next one is enriquez  and what are the dates there it's the  end of october so 27 29th of october  okay and uh richard is also sort of the  originator of these polyglot gatherings  or conferences because the first one was  in  budapest budapest was the first one what  year was actually kindly supported yes  that was five years ago now five years  ago and then you've had it in  thessaloniki yes and there's there's  another it's called called the gathering  which was in berlin and then in  bratislava and now we have here  and i  at some level we all hope that uh  you know what what i call the polyglot  ghetto which is all the cleaners that  somehow this will expand into the  broader community and encourage people  to learn languages and i would encourage  you to participate in any polyglot  conference gathering that may be taking  place near you yeah i think it's  infectious you know the whole the  environment is infectious people uh are  genuinely very open  and whether you're on your first or your  21st language it doesn't really matter  exactly and you we all learn from each  other  you know yep absolutely and we don't  judge each other  okay bye bye  [Music]  you

